WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.179
Hey remember this unicorn. We're going

00:00:03.179 --> 00:00:13.110
to talk more about set up and pay off

00:00:13.110 --> 00:00:15.150
A couple days ago I got this comment in

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:17.460
response to the Suicide Squad review, so

00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:20.100
let's quickly do a clearer dive into

00:00:20.100 --> 00:00:23.100
what's really the essence of setup and

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:25.500
pay off. Now in the previous video I

00:00:25.500 --> 00:00:27.449
mentioned the rule of threes where an

00:00:27.449 --> 00:00:29.250
element will be set up then there's a

00:00:29.250 --> 00:00:32.340
reminder and then finally a payoff. This

00:00:32.340 --> 00:00:33.780
idea meshes with another dramatic

00:00:33.780 --> 00:00:36.480
principle of Chekhov's Gun. Anton

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:39.090
Chekhov was a prolific Russian author

00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:41.250
and playwright in the mid late eighteen

00:00:41.250 --> 00:00:43.620
hundreds. He believed strongly in

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:45.750
narrative efficiency and thought stories

00:00:45.750 --> 00:00:47.670
should have formal rules of construction

00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:50.250
which is why we have the phrase

00:00:50.250 --> 00:00:52.410
Chekhov's Gun. Remove everything that has no

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:54.390
relevance to the story. If you say in the

00:00:54.390 --> 00:00:55.949
first chapter that there is a rifle

00:00:55.949 --> 00:00:57.719
hanging on the wall, in the second or

00:00:57.719 --> 00:01:00.000
third chapter it absolutely must go off.

00:01:00.000 --> 00:01:02.070
If it's not going to be fired

00:01:02.070 --> 00:01:04.049
it shouldn't be hanging there.

00:01:04.049 --> 00:01:06.840
The unicorn in Suicide Squad is unusual, it's an

00:01:06.840 --> 00:01:08.700
absurdist element, it breaks from

00:01:08.700 --> 00:01:11.220
expectations, and thus definitionally

00:01:11.220 --> 00:01:12.869
calls attention to itself

00:01:12.869 --> 00:01:15.600
This is why we, or at least I, expect

00:01:15.600 --> 00:01:17.009
something to come of it.

00:01:17.009 --> 00:01:18.270
Now let's go back and look at that

00:01:18.270 --> 00:01:20.520
comment. Wouldn't the title card be the

00:01:20.520 --> 00:01:22.650
intro when we first see it the reminder

00:01:22.650 --> 00:01:26.159
and then the fight the payoff? Now the

00:01:26.159 --> 00:01:28.020
comment makes a critical error in

00:01:28.020 --> 00:01:30.119
evaluating the rule of threes which is

00:01:30.119 --> 00:01:33.900
holding too tightly to the idea of three

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:35.790
The idea isn't just that something

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:38.700
should show up three times but as per

00:01:38.700 --> 00:01:41.280
Chekhov's gun it should do something

00:01:41.280 --> 00:01:43.470
Even though the unicorn appears or is

00:01:43.470 --> 00:01:45.570
referenced three different times

00:01:45.570 --> 00:01:47.579
none of these actually come to anything

00:01:47.579 --> 00:01:50.490
Three is really just a convenient number

00:01:50.490 --> 00:01:52.439
it has a good rhythm and once something

00:01:52.439 --> 00:01:54.270
has happened three times in a row we

00:01:54.270 --> 00:01:56.460
instinctively start to feel like it is

00:01:56.460 --> 00:01:59.040
intentional rather than random. Three is

00:01:59.040 --> 00:02:01.380
indicative of a pattern. Even simpler

00:02:01.380 --> 00:02:03.210
than the psychology of patterns though

00:02:03.210 --> 00:02:05.579
is just basic information juggling:

00:02:05.579 --> 00:02:08.129
managing the human memory. If someone is

00:02:08.129 --> 00:02:10.470
watching a movie or a play or television

00:02:10.470 --> 00:02:13.010
they're actually taking in a lot of

00:02:13.010 --> 00:02:15.080
information at a more or less constant rate for

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:17.420
upwards of several hours. The reminder

00:02:17.420 --> 00:02:19.220
stage of the rule of threes is really

00:02:19.220 --> 00:02:20.930
just about helping the audience keep

00:02:20.930 --> 00:02:22.819
track of something set up in the first

00:02:22.819 --> 00:02:25.069
20 minutes if it's not going to be relevant

00:02:25.069 --> 00:02:27.860
for another two hours. If the span of

00:02:27.860 --> 00:02:30.110
time between setup and payoff is much

00:02:30.110 --> 00:02:32.180
shorter then there's no need for a

00:02:32.180 --> 00:02:34.220
reminder because it's still fresh in the

00:02:34.220 --> 00:02:35.480
audience's mind

00:02:35.480 --> 00:02:37.549
while if the time between is much much

00:02:37.549 --> 00:02:39.829
longer then either you'll need more

00:02:39.829 --> 00:02:41.780
reminders or you'll just need to spend

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:43.549
more time embedding it in the

00:02:43.549 --> 00:02:45.739
audience's memory. But even that still

00:02:45.739 --> 00:02:47.870
isn't getting to the heart of the issue

00:02:47.870 --> 00:02:50.060
and to do that we're going to take a

00:02:50.060 --> 00:02:51.829
look at an episode of The Simpsons.

00:02:51.829 --> 00:02:54.920
Season three, Bart's Friend Falls in Love

00:02:54.920 --> 00:02:57.079
centers around Bart and Milhouse having

00:02:57.079 --> 00:02:58.819
a falling out over the new girl in class

00:02:58.819 --> 00:03:01.790
At the start of the episode Milhouse shows

00:03:01.790 --> 00:03:04.099
Bart his new magic 8-ball, they ask it

00:03:04.099 --> 00:03:05.629
several questions, and the 8-ball

00:03:05.629 --> 00:03:07.489
predicts that they won't be friends by

00:03:07.489 --> 00:03:08.840
the end of the day.

00:03:08.840 --> 00:03:11.810
Sure enough Milhouse falls in love with

00:03:11.810 --> 00:03:13.940
Samantha, the new girl in class.

00:03:13.940 --> 00:03:15.260
Bart resents the change in his

00:03:15.260 --> 00:03:17.030
relationship with Milhouse and the two

00:03:17.030 --> 00:03:19.069
have a falling out the culminating Bart

00:03:19.069 --> 00:03:21.260
stitching on Samantha to her father who

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:22.849
has her transferred to a private girls'

00:03:22.849 --> 00:03:25.370
school. Feeling guilty about the grief

00:03:25.370 --> 00:03:27.410
he's caused Milhouse, Bart confesses to

00:03:27.410 --> 00:03:30.169
Milhouse and Milhouse attacks him. Bart

00:03:30.169 --> 00:03:32.060
grabs the eight ball and hits Milhouse

00:03:32.060 --> 00:03:36.710
in the head breaking it

00:03:36.710 --> 00:03:39.170
So this is all over within a half hour

00:03:39.170 --> 00:03:41.450
including commercial breaks so there's

00:03:41.450 --> 00:03:44.000
not really any pressing need for a

00:03:44.000 --> 00:03:46.340
reminder, just the setup and the payoff.

00:03:46.340 --> 00:03:48.710
The setup is that the introduction of

00:03:48.710 --> 00:03:50.090
the eight ball into the relationship

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:52.790
heralds the forming of a rift, while the

00:03:52.790 --> 00:03:54.620
payoff is that the violence and

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:56.900
destruction of the eight ball marks the

00:03:56.900 --> 00:03:59.330
healing of that rift. A peaceful, friendly

00:03:59.330 --> 00:04:01.520
interaction with the eight ball moves

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:05.240
the emotional state into chaos; a chaotic

00:04:05.240 --> 00:04:08.300
violent interaction moves the emotional

00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:11.180
state into peace. The eight ball being

00:04:11.180 --> 00:04:13.130
used for its intended purpose brings

00:04:13.130 --> 00:04:15.710
discord, brings a prophecy that dooms the

00:04:15.710 --> 00:04:17.960
protagonists, and the destruction of the

00:04:17.960 --> 00:04:20.600
eight ball, using it as a weapon breaks

00:04:20.600 --> 00:04:22.610
the curse and breaks the power of the

00:04:22.610 --> 00:04:24.890
eight ball over the relationship.

00:04:24.890 --> 00:04:26.750
the writer could have used anything for this

00:04:26.750 --> 00:04:29.780
gag but by using the 8-ball it forms an

00:04:29.780 --> 00:04:32.450
emotionally satisfying loop which is the

00:04:32.450 --> 00:04:34.850
essence of payoff. A stuffed unicorn

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:38.060
flying out of Boomerang's jacket isn't

00:04:38.060 --> 00:04:52.240
emotionally satisfying

